Real fix lives in retrieval, not the prompt — the live chat agent's scoped-retriever thresholds (the 0.6/0.55 tiering + rerank in SessionAgentManager.buildAgent) are dropping exact-token docs that sit at 0.55–0.60 similarity. Options: lower/there tune the tier-1 floor, ensure the lexical/hybrid path, or verify the reranker isn't evicting the covering doc.

Think of the assistant answering in two stages: first it fetches the handful of documentation snippets it thinks are relevant, then it writes an answer from them. My earlier change tried to fix the writing stage. But the problem is the fetching stage — the right snippet never gets pulled, so there's nothing to write from.

Here's the mechanism. When the fetcher scores how well a document matches the question, it gives a number between 0 and 1 (higher = better match). The system is configured to throw away anything scoring below 0.60 on the first pass. The VIN document scored 0.5811 — just under that line — so it got discarded before the assistant ever saw it. Exact-token questions (a bare code, a VIN, a part number) tend to land in exactly this 0.55–0.60 dead zone: the document genuinely contains the answer, but the "meaning-similarity" score comes out mediocre because the question is just a literal string with little semantic richness to match on.

Three ways to fix that, roughly in order of bluntness:

Lower the 0.60 cutoff so near-miss documents survive — simplest, but risks letting in more noise across the board.
Make the exact-word search actually kick in for these bare-token questions. That's the feature from issue #1124 that's built but switched off — it matches literal strings instead of meaning, which is exactly what these queries need. This ties the two threads together: item 4's bug is real-world evidence for why that feature should be turned on.
Check the re-ranker. Even when the right document survives the first cut, a later "re-sort the finalists" step might be bumping it out of the top few that actually get shown. Worth confirming it isn't the culprit before touching thresholds.
